@startuml
title
    Keyple - FSM Sequence Diagram: Card Insertion, synchronous observer (REPEATING mode) - keyple-service-java-lib
end title

' == THEME ==

'Couleurs issues de : https://htmlcolorcodes.com/fr/tableau-de-couleur/tableau-de-couleur-design-plat/
!define C_GREY1 F8F9F9
!define C_GREY2 F2F3F4
!define C_GREY3 E5E7E9
!define C_GREY4 D7DBDD
!define C_GREY5 CACFD2
!define C_GREY6 BDC3C7
!define C_LINK 3498DB
!define C_USE 27AE60

' Thread color palette (used on activation bars)
!define T_APP  AED6F1
!define T_MON  FAD7A0

skinparam BackgroundColor #C_GREY1
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

skinparam participant {
    BackgroundColor #EBF5FB
}
skinparam actor {
    BackgroundColor #FEFECE
    BorderColor #D4AC0D
    BorderThickness 2
}
skinparam sequence {
    ArrowThickness 2
    ArrowColor #2C3E50
    LifeLineBorderColor #3498DB
    LifeLineBorderThickness 2
    GroupBorderThickness 2
    GroupBorderColor #BDC3C7
    DividerBorderThickness 2
    DividerBorderColor #BDC3C7
}
skinparam note {
    BackgroundColor #FEFECE
    BorderColor #D4AC0D
}

' == CONTENT ==

legend right
    __Thread color coding__ :
    * <back:#AED6F1>  Application Thread   </back>
    * <back:#FAD7A0>  Monitoring Thread    </back>

    __Key properties of the SingleThreadExecutor__ :
    * A single background thread executes all monitoring jobs sequentially.
    * If a new job is submitted while the thread is busy, it is **queued**.
    * The queued job starts only once the current job's run() returns.

    __Key consequence of the synchronous observer__ :
    * The observer runs on the monitoring thread, which holds the FSM lock.
    * finalizeCardProcessing() re-enters the lock (Java synchronized is re-entrant).
    * switchState() submits the next monitoring job, but the executor thread is still
      busy — the job is queued and will start only after fire(CARD_INSERTED) returns.
end legend

actor "Application" as App #FEFECE
participant "CardReaderObserverSpi\n(observer)" as Observer #FEFECE

participant "ObservableLocalReaderAdapter" as Adapter #EBF5FB
participant "FsmService\n<<synchronized>>" as FSM #EBF5FB
participant "FsmState" as State #EBF5FB

box "SingleThreadExecutor" #FAD7A0
    participant "FsmJobActive\n(insertion)" as Job #EBF5FB
    participant "FsmJob\n(removal)" as NewJob #EBF5FB
end box

participant "ObservableReaderSpi\n(hardware)" as Spi #FDEDEC

' ─── startCardDetection ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

== startCardDetection (Application Thread) — identical to the async scenario ==

App -> Adapter : startCardDetection(REPEATING)
activate Adapter #T_APP
Adapter -> FSM : fire(CARD_DETECTION_START_REQUESTED)
activate FSM #T_APP
note right of FSM : **synchronized** — acquires FSM lock
FSM -> State : onTrigger(CARD_DETECTION_START_REQUESTED)
activate State #T_APP
note right of State : current state:\nWAIT_FOR_START_DETECTION
State -> FSM : switchState(WAIT_FOR_CARD_INSERTION)
activate FSM #T_APP
note right of FSM : deactivates WaitForStartDetection\nactivates WaitForCardInsertion
FSM -> Job : submit getTask()
activate Job #T_MON
note right : Called from FsmState.onActivate()\nMonitoring job starts in background executor thread
FSM -> Spi : onStartDetection()
note right : Called from\nWaitForCardInsertion.onActivate()
FSM --> State
deactivate FSM
State --> FSM
deactivate State
FSM --> Adapter
deactivate FSM
Adapter --> App
deactivate Adapter

' ─── Card detection loop ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

== Card detection (Monitoring Thread) — identical to the async scenario ==

loop until card detected
    Job -> Spi : isCardPresent()
    activate Spi
    Spi --> Job : false
    deactivate Spi
    Job -> Job : sleep(pollIntervalMs)
end
note over Spi : Card inserted
Job -> Spi : isCardPresent()
activate Spi
Spi --> Job : true
deactivate Spi

' ─── CARD_INSERTED trigger ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────

== CARD_INSERTED trigger (Monitoring Thread — FSM lock acquired) ==

Job -> State : fire(CARD_INSERTED)
activate State #T_MON
note right of State : FsmState.fire() — delegates\nto service.fire()

State -> FSM : fire(CARD_INSERTED)
activate FSM #T_MON
note right of FSM : **synchronized** — acquires FSM lock\nMonitoring thread holds this lock\nuntil fire() returns

FSM -> State : onTrigger(CARD_INSERTED)
activate State #T_MON
note right of State : current state:\nWAIT_FOR_CARD_INSERTION

State -> Adapter : processCardInserted()
activate Adapter #T_MON
Adapter -> Spi : transmit card selection requests
activate Spi
Spi --> Adapter : card selection responses
deactivate Spi
Adapter --> State : CardReaderEvent
deactivate Adapter

State -> FSM : switchState(WAIT_FOR_CARD_PROCESSING)
activate FSM #T_MON
note right of FSM : FsmState.onDeactivate() called\non WaitForCardInsertion —\nthen WaitForCardProcessing activated
FSM -> Job : stop()
activate Job #T_MON
note right : running = false\nMonitoring thread continues\nexecuting fire()
Job --> FSM
deactivate Job
FSM -> FSM : monitoringTask.cancel(true)
note right : Interrupt flag set on monitoring thread\n(no immediate effect — thread is executing\nsynchronized code, not sleeping)
FSM --> State
deactivate FSM

' ── Synchronous observer call ─────────────────────────────────────────────────

State -> Adapter : notifyObservers(CardReaderEvent)
activate Adapter #T_MON
note right of Adapter : **Synchronous dispatch** —\ncalls onReaderEvent() directly\non the monitoring thread

Adapter -> Observer : onReaderEvent(CARD_INSERTED event)
activate Observer #T_MON
note right of Observer : **Runs on monitoring thread**\nFSM lock is still held by this thread

note over Observer : Business logic\n(e.g. ticketing application\nprocesses the card)

' ── finalizeCardProcessing called by observer ─────────────────────────────────

Observer -> Adapter : finalizeCardProcessing()
activate Adapter #T_MON

Adapter -> FSM : fire(CARD_PROCESSING_ENDED)
activate FSM #T_MON
note right of FSM : **synchronized — re-entrant**\nSame thread already holds the FSM lock\n→ enters the block without blocking

FSM -> State : onTrigger(CARD_PROCESSING_ENDED)
activate State #T_MON
note right of State : current state:\nWAIT_FOR_CARD_PROCESSING\n[REPEATING] → switchState(WAIT_FOR_CARD_REMOVAL)

State -> FSM : switchState(WAIT_FOR_CARD_REMOVAL)
activate FSM #T_MON
note right of FSM : deactivates WaitForCardProcessing\nactivates WaitForCardRemoval:\n  executorService.submit(newJob.getTask())\n⚠ Executor's single thread IS currently\n  executing this job → new task is QUEUED,\n  not started yet

FSM -> NewJob : submit getTask()
note right : ⚠ Task queued\nExecutor thread is busy —\nwill start after run() returns

FSM --> State
deactivate FSM
State --> FSM
deactivate State

FSM --> Adapter
deactivate FSM

Adapter --> Observer
deactivate Adapter

Observer --> Adapter : (onReaderEvent returns)
deactivate Observer

Adapter --> State : (notifyObservers returns)
deactivate Adapter

State --> FSM
deactivate State

FSM --> State : (service.fire() returns)
deactivate FSM

State --> Job : (state.fire() returns)
deactivate State

note over Job : run() exits —\nExecutor thread is now free\nQueued job can start

deactivate Job

' ─── Next monitoring job ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────

== Next monitoring job starts (same executor thread) ==

activate NewJob #T_MON
note over NewJob : SingleThreadExecutor dequeues\nand starts the removal job\n(FsmJobActive or FsmJobPassive\ndepending on the SPI)

NewJob -> Spi : isCardPresent() / waitForCardRemoval()
activate Spi
note right : Monitoring for card removal
Spi --> NewJob
deactivate Spi

@enduml
